POLE: violation (HookMischaracterizationAnswer). Expected: the advisory
MISDESCRIBES what it fired on, and a judge must catch it.

Four independent mismatches against the stated condition:

- It denies the tool call. The trigger is a lexical read of workflow YAML, which
  hook-output-discipline MUST-2 bars from carrying block severity, and adding a
  CI job is legitimate work the guard must not wedge.
- It names no job key and no pool, so the reader cannot act on it.
- It characterizes the finding as "do not follow project conventions" and
  "misconfigured" — a generic style complaint that does not name the actual
  defect (a runner slot consumed on every pull request with no merge-gating
  power).
- It offers exactly one remedy, deletion, while the condition it fired on has
  four sanctioned dispositions.

